---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [{ params: { locale: "en" } }];
}
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Privacy Policy - Utildesk"
  description="Privacy information for Utildesk, hosting, analytics and external resources."
  robots="noindex,nofollow,noarchive,nosnippet"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://tools.utildesk.de/en/privacy/" />
    <meta name="googlebot" content="noindex,nofollow,noarchive,nosnippet" />
    <meta name="bingbot" content="noindex,nofollow,noarchive,nosnippet" />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="tool-akte sheet-wrap legal-sheet legal-sheet-plain">
    <nav class="akte-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/en/">Back to directory</a>
      <span class="akte-crumb-sep">/</span>
      <span class="akte-crumb-current">Privacy</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="sheet-head">
      <div class="sheet-head-kicker">legal / privacy</div>
      <h1 class="sheet-head-h1">Privacy Policy<span class="akte-mast-dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="sheet-head-dek">
        This English version summarizes the German privacy policy for international readers.
        The German version remains the primary legal text.
      </p>
      <div class="sheet-head-meta">
        <span><strong>Last updated:</strong> 31 July 2026</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>Noindex, not intended for search discovery</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="akte-article legal-article">
      <div class="akte-article-body legal-prose">
        <div>
          <h2>1. Controller</h2>
          <p>
            The controller is the operator named in the <a href="/impressum/">German Impressum</a>,
            which also provides the postal address and direct email contact.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Technical access data and Cloudflare</h2>
          <p>
            A page request necessarily transmits connection data such as IP address, timestamp,
            requested URL, referrer, browser/operating-system information and HTTP status. Utildesk is
            delivered through Cloudflare Pages and Cloudflare Pages Functions. Cloudflare, Inc. acts as
            a recipient and processor for delivery, security, DDoS protection and troubleshooting.
            Processing is based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cloudflare may process data outside the EEA. According to Cloudflare, transfers to the
            United States rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and, where required, the EU Standard
            Contractual Clauses with supplementary measures.
          </p>

          <h2>3. Logs, cookies and local storage</h2>
          <p>
            Server and security logs are used only for delivery, troubleshooting, abuse prevention and
            security. They are deleted, anonymised or overwritten when no longer needed, unless an
            incident or legal obligation requires longer retention.
          </p>
          <p>
            The public site does not set marketing cookies. <code>localStorage</code> can retain
            <code>utildesk-theme</code>, <code>utildesk-design</code>,
            <code>utildesk-tools-view</code>, <code>utildesk-tools-sort</code> and
            <code>utildesk-analytics-consent-v1</code> to remember choices expressly made by the
            visitor. The protected editorial area uses the strictly necessary session cookie
            <code>utildesk_ratgeber_review</code>.
          </p>

          <h2>4. Optional Umami analytics</h2>
          <p>
            The self-hosted, cookie-free Umami tracker on <code>stats.utildesk.de</code> is loaded only
            after the visitor chooses “Allow statistics”. The legal bases are consent under Article
            6(1)(a) GDPR and Section 25(1) TDDDG. Without consent, the analytics script is not loaded.
          </p>
          <p>
            Umami may process page URL and title, referrer, timestamp, language, browser, operating
            system, device type, screen resolution and approximate country or region. The IP address
            is used for technical processing and coarse location but, according to Umami, is not
            stored. Utildesk also records a <code>qualified-reader</code> event after a trusted
            interaction, at least 45 seconds reading time and at least 50 percent scroll depth. It
            stores page type, language and threshold values, not the content of user input.
          </p>
          <p>
            Consent can be changed at any time through “Privacy settings” in the footer. Withdrawal
            does not affect processing that was lawful before withdrawal.
          </p>

          <h2>5. External resources and links</h2>
          <p>
            The site loads Google Fonts and may request missing tool favicons from Google, DuckDuckGo
            or Icon.Horse. The visitor's IP address and technical request information are transferred
            to the relevant provider. This is based on the legitimate interest in a readable and
            recognisable directory under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Providers outside the EEA may rely on
            adequacy decisions or Standard Contractual Clauses.
          </p>
          <p>
            Tool entries and guides can contain affiliate or referral links. The destination provider
            processes a request under its own privacy policy only after the visitor follows the link.
            Utildesk does not set its own marketing cookie for this purpose.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Machine-readable and editorial endpoints</h2>
          <p>
            Utildesk provides feeds, JSON APIs, Markdown mirrors and <code>llms.txt</code> manifests. These
            endpoints create the same technical access data as regular page views. The protected
            Ratgeber review area stores drafts, images, metadata and status information in Cloudflare
            KV and is protected by authentication and technical tokens.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            If a visitor contacts Utildesk, the sender address, message, time and voluntarily supplied
            information are processed to handle the request. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR
            for contractual or pre-contractual matters and otherwise Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Recipients, transfers and retention</h2>
          <p>
            Data is disclosed only to recipients needed for the stated purposes, especially Cloudflare,
            providers of requested external resources and communication or infrastructure providers.
            International transfers rely, where required, on an adequacy decision, Standard Contractual
            Clauses and supplementary measures.
          </p>
          <p>
            Personal data is retained only while the relevant purpose exists. Contact data is deleted
            after the request is resolved unless retention duties apply. Security data can be retained
            until an incident is resolved. Analytics data is deleted or aggregated when no longer
            needed for audience comparison and service improvement. Local preferences remain on the
            visitor's device until deleted by the visitor or browser.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Subject to the statutory conditions, data subjects have rights of access, rectification,
            erasure, restriction, portability and objection under Articles 15–21 GDPR. Consent may be
            withdrawn at any time with future effect. A complaint can be lodged under Article 77 GDPR,
            including with the State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information of
            North Rhine-Westphalia, <a href="https://www.ldi.nrw.de/" rel="nofollow noopener">www.ldi.nrw.de</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Required data and automated decisions</h2>
          <p>
            The website cannot be delivered without technically necessary connection data. All other
            information is voluntary. Utildesk does not make solely automated decisions that produce
            legal or similarly significant effects.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Updates</h2>
          <p>This policy may be updated when the website, infrastructure or legal requirements change.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
